The end-to-end script passes, including LLVM execution and `#Top`. I’m adding two small bridge claims so the proof file explicitly checks that the exact translated public/helper closures enter the inductive proof marker; this makes the connection between implementation bodies and the universal recurrence visible to `kprove`, not just explanatory.
